                },
                "title": {
                  "S": "Miss"
                },
                "impact": {
                  "S": "Beyond the Degree — My Experience\nAttending Beyond the Degree was truly an eye-opener for me. Here are the key things I took away:\nBalancing CGPA with Business\nYou don't have to choose between your grades and building something. With the right mindset and structure, both can thrive side by side.\nManaging Your Time\nTime is your most valuable asset as a student. Learning how to plan your day and protect your hours is what separates those who just get by from those who get ahead.\nKnowing What You Want\nBefore you can build anything meaningful, you need clarity. When you know your direction, every decision becomes easier.\nBuilding Valuable Relationships\nNot just networking — real connections. The people you meet and invest in genuinely will open doors that no certificate ever could.\nWhy Skills and Certification Outperform\nA degree shows you can learn. Skills show you can do. Certifications give you proof. In today's world, proof of ability matters more than the paper on your wall.\nFinding Leverage\nDiscover what you do better than most and lean into it. That is your edge.\nLearn to Solve Problems\nPeople pay for solutions. If you can walk into a room and fix something others can't, you will never be without opportunity.\nGet Visible as Quickly as Possible\nDon't wait until you feel ready. Share your work, show up, and let people know what you're building. Visibility creates opportunities."
                },
